Visibility annotations inside a class (diag.visibility_annotation,
warning): class methods are always Public|Virtual, so /*@private; and
/*@protected; are inert there, even in the exact form. The info-tier
visibility_annotation_usage must not double-report them.
-- input.ssl --
:CLASS Renderer;
:DECLARE sBuffer;

/*@private;
:PROCEDURE Flush;
	Me:sBuffer := "";
:ENDPROC;

/*@protected;
:PROCEDURE Append;
	:PARAMETERS sText;
	Me:sBuffer += sText;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:CLASS Renderer;
:DECLARE sBuffer;

/*@private;
:PROCEDURE Flush;
	Me:sBuffer := "";
:ENDPROC;

/*@protected;
:PROCEDURE Append;
	:PARAMETERS sText;
	Me:sBuffer += sText;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
4:1-4:12 warning visibility_annotation: Visibility annotation '/*@private;' has no effect on class methods — class methods are always public/virtual
9:1-9:14 warning visibility_annotation: Visibility annotation '/*@protected;' has no effect on class methods — class methods are always public/virtual
